# Website screenshots (canonical format)

When updating homepage / marketing-site screenshots for new features, **match the currently live format**. Do not invent a new framing style.

## Canonical asset

- **Path:** `public/screenshots/*.png` (deployed copy: `docs/screenshots/`)
- **Content:** App UI only — status bar + Dynamic Island included in the capture
- **Not in the PNG:** device chassis/bezel, store headlines, disclaimers, cream marketing canvas
- **Size:** **414 × 900** PNG (RGBA), ~ same aspect as iPhone raw `1320×2868`
- **Background:** app cream (`#F7F6F3`), full-bleed screen capture

## How the phone look is made

`PhoneShot` (`src/components/phone-shot.tsx`) draws the dark green CSS bezel + shadow around these raw UI images. **Do not** bake a second bezel into the PNG (that double-frames).

## Source → site

1. Capture / refresh `barem/store_assets/screenshots/raw/ios/` (full-res)
2. Export site size into `public/screenshots/` (same filenames `01_home.png` … `07_profile.png`):

```bash
# from barem-site, or see README 「스크린샷」
../barem/tool/export_site_screenshots.sh
```

3. `npm run deploy` → commit `public/screenshots` + `docs`

## Rejected formats (do not use on the site)

- Store marketing composites (`barem/store_assets/screenshots/ios/` with headlines)
- Bezel-only Pillow frames pasted as the site PNG while also using CSS PhoneShot
- Dropping raw 1320×2868 without resizing (oversized; break `PhoneShot` width/height contract)
